<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Justo Rufino Barrios</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1835–1885</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Justo Rufino Barrios was a Guatemalan general who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberal-revolution-of-1871">Liberal Revolution of 1871</a> and ruled as president from 1873 to 1885. He expropriated church lands, expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a> and built roads, railways and schools. His promotion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> estates relied on forced Maya labour. He was killed in battle trying to reunite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a> by force.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/justo-rufino-barrios.jpg" alt="Justo Rufino Barrios" width="320" height="485" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Justo_Rufino_Barrios_Auy%C3%B3n.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
